From: ITSMEFRTRUST <215584995+ITSMEFRTRUST@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:39:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 084/138] misc: Add a timed wakeup for suspend-to-idle without
 an RTC alarm

Nothing can wake an Apple A8 running Linux on a timer: the PMU's alarm
and its interrupt line (AP GPIO 106) have no driver. The tick, however,
keeps running in suspend-to-idle there, because the only idle state
(WFI) has no ->enter_s2idle and the tick is never frozen. An hrtimer
still fires while the system is suspended.

Add a small driver that arms an hrtimer in the noirq suspend phase when
/sys/module/s2idle_wake_timer/parameters/wake_after_ms is non-zero and
reports a hard wakeup event when it expires. It ends suspend-to-idle the
way a wake interrupt does, and its wakeup source shows up in
/sys/class/wakeup. Inert while the parameter is 0.

It is the safety net for the first suspend tests (the phone comes back
even if no wake interrupt works), gives fixed-length suspends for
battery measurements, and lets userspace wake up periodically.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
